# Random modules as in random-classes-1.test, with existentially typed
# functions too, whose results only their existential constraints and
# polymorphic callees accept, and rarely two calls' types in one list,
# which is a type error (generate-random-programs.py --existentials).
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-random-programs.py --existentials --seed 3 --count 60 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --allow-errors %t/*.m
